From e39e411dc2e0cd2de725fe38744dc248df5bfdfc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 12:10:39 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] d/wmr: Survive transient companion device drops during
 startup

The HP Reverb G2's companion HID device (03f0:0580) routinely drops off
the USB bus and re-enumerates while the headset display powers up (the
same fault is observable under Windows, where its audio function appears
and disappears - it is a physical-layer weakness of the G2 cable/board).

Two consequences inside the driver:

1. control_read_packets() treated any os_hid_read error as fatal and
   returned false, which breaks the whole wmr_run_thread read loop -
   killing the HMD IMU feed and all tunnelled controller packet delivery
   over an unrelated, transient companion hiccup. Log at debug level and
   keep the thread alive instead.

2. The screen-enable command sent during wmr_hmd_activate_reverb() can be
   silently lost if the companion device drops right around activation
   (HID_SEND only logs on failure). Re-send it after the settle sleep;
   the command is idempotent.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_hmd.c | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_hmd.c b/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_hmd.c
index 0e7da4619..2f10ff344 100644
--- a/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_hmd.c
+++ b/src/xrt/drivers/wmr/wmr_hmd.c
@@ -586,9 +586,12 @@ control_read_packets(struct wmr_hmd *wh)
 	os_mutex_unlock(&wh->hid_lock);
 
 	if (size < 0) {
-		WMR_ERROR(wh, "Error reading from companion (HMD control) device. Call to os_hid_read returned %i",
+		// The companion device can transiently drop off and re-enumerate while the
+		// headset display is powering up. Don't kill the whole read thread (which
+		// also drives tracking camera/IMU reads) over a read error here.
+		WMR_DEBUG(wh, "Error reading from companion (HMD control) device. Call to os_hid_read returned %i",
 		          size);
-		return false;
+		return true;
 	}
 	if (size == 0) {
 		WMR_TRACE(wh, "No more data to read");
@@ -779,6 +782,11 @@ wmr_hmd_activate_reverb(struct wmr_hmd *wh)
 	uint64_t seconds = debug_get_num_option_sleep_seconds();
 	os_nanosleep(U_TIME_1S_IN_NS * seconds);
 
+	// The companion HID device can transiently drop off and re-enumerate right around
+	// activation, which can silently lose the screen-enable command sent above. Resend it
+	// now that things have had time to settle, so the panel doesn't stay stuck off/blank.
+	wmr_hmd_screen_enable_reverb(wh, wh->hmd_screen_enable);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
